# BASIS CHOICE. Everything here is 6-31G*, not the 6-311+G** of the QM/MM site
# energies. A mixed-basis attempt (opt at 6-311+G**, Hessian at 6-31G*) FAILED:
# TeraChem refused the Hessian with "maximum component of gradient is too large"
# because a geometry stationary in one basis is not stationary in another
# (Grad-Max 2.20e-4 at 6-311+G** vs 6.45e-3 at 6-31G*). A Hessian requires a
# stationary point IN ITS OWN BASIS, so the whole chain must share one.
# 6-31G* is chosen for speed; omega and the Huang-Rhys factor S are far less
# basis sensitive than excitation energies. This must be stated wherever the
# resulting S and omega are used.
# Stage 2: numerical Hessian (6N displacements) at the optimised geometry.
coordinates optim.xyz
run frequencies
method camb3lyp
basis 6-31gs
# SPEED: Hessian at 6-31G* rather than 6-311+G**. 264 finite-difference
# gradients dominate the wall time, and mode frequencies / Huang-Rhys factors
# are far less basis sensitive than excitation energies. The optimisation and
# the excited-state gradient stay at 6-311+G**.
charge -1
spinmult 1
scrdir scr_freq
scf diis+a
threall 1.0e-13
convthre 1.0e-6
gpus 1
end
